<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan gold rates seen rising in Ramadan.</title>
<headline>Pakistan gold rates seen rising in Ramadan.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan gold rates are likely to rise gradually before the Moslem fasting month of Ramadan starting next month, dealers said on Monday.</p>
<p>Demand for jewellery rises in Ramadan and that pushes the prices of gold up in the domestic markets, one dealer said.</p>
<p>Silver rates had almost been stabilised as there was no demand for it for jewellery purpose, the dealer said.</p>
<p>    Gold 24 carat in rupees per 10 grammes SUN	Dec 15</p>
<p>							 5,155    5,130</p>
<p>    Silver per 1,000 grammes		   7,286    7,286</p>
<p>($1=40.22 rupees) -- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
